Subject: [loglanists] The Loglan Institute's New CEO

I am pleased to announce that Robert McIvor has accepted the position
of CEO of the Loglan Institute, and will assume his duties immediately.
Bob is a longtime loglanist, the chief grammarian of the Institute, and a
frequent contributor to this list.  He succeeds Alex Leith,  who passed
away earlier this year.

Loglan is an artificial human language designed by James Cooke Brown
in the late 1950's.

Wes Parsons
President, The Loglan Institute



           
